@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Urgent narrow lineage: SEN0414 chapters 10 and 11, one code, one environment"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.30.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1011simp-lineage/1.30.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1011simp_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.30.0 (2026-11-24): The chapter 10 concept panel story is done. All 36 Try it runs of the 59 concept panels are the book's lines (or named programs of the chapter source) with a hidden set-up, and the Lab pane Chapter examples (the old transcript) is left out; page 9.22.0 passes the full page test."""@en .

ex:TK11_Concepts_10_Build backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "New files: A-box 03-materials/ch10/rdodi/sen0414_ch10_domain_abox_v1_0_2.ttl (made by 08-tooling/try_it_abox_make_v1_0_0.py from 08-tooling/ch10-page/try_it_ch10_v1_0_0.json: the I/O example of each of 36 concepts replaced; every other line copied), set-ups 08-tooling/ch10-page/try_it_setup_v1_0_0.json, page data tool 2.30.0, template 9.53.7 (runs a hidden set-up before the shown code), page test 9.40.0 (a result of several lines is checked by what it prints), page 03-materials/ch10/page/sen0414_ch10_page_v9_22_0.html. Each Try it code is a line or block of the book chapter read from the book file (the book column of the JSON names it) or the chapter source program that holds it; the book's Windows paths and drive folders become relative paths in the page's own working folder, and the dbm stand-in of the source is reused for shelve. The Lab pane Chapter examples (18 entries of the old transcript) is left out because the Chapter code tab holds the same programs. Page 9.21.0, A-box 1.0.1, template 9.53.6, page data 2.29.0 and page test 9.39.0 stay unchanged." .
ex:TK11_Concepts_10_Verify backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Logs in 08-tooling/ch10-page/logs_v9_22_0: code check C1 to C5 0 findings (18 examples); full page test 9.40.0 in a browser: exit 0, 406 features passed, 0 failed, widgets 59 of 59 (every Try it ran, was edited, reset and shown in the detail card). A first run with test 9.39.0 failed two widgets because their result has several lines and the one-line prediction field cannot hold them; the test was changed for that and nothing else (9.40.0). Open: the outputs are recorded under Linux (PosixPath where the book shows WindowsPath)." .
ex:ST11_Concepts_10 backlog:hasState backlog:Done ;
    backlog:hasAuditNote "Criterion met for chapter 10: every Try it run of the concept panels is the book's code with its hidden set-up, runs in the browser and the page test passes. The three concepts without a run (shelf backend, shelf security, quiz data) keep their recorded text." .
